        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">How psychodynamic therapy works</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">Sessions do not follow a set agenda; you are free to speak about whatever comes to mind. The psychologist notices recurring themes and emotional patterns, and makes sense of them together with you. If you are looking for more structured, short-term work, <a href="/en/services/cbt-therapy.html" class="text-primary hover:underline">CBT</a> may be the better fit.</p>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">The Unconscious at Work</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Feelings and conflicts we are unaware of can quietly steer our choices and relationships.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Early Relationships</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Attachment patterns learned in our first relationships shape how much closeness and distance we need today.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">The Therapeutic Relationship</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Patterns from outside appear in the consulting room too — a unique opportunity to work with them safely.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Lasting Change</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">The aim is not only symptom relief but a lasting expansion of your capacity to understand yourself.</p>
          </div>
